.TH SWIFTJ2K-CLI 1 "October 28, 2026" "12.1.0" "Swift Image Compression Suite"
.SH NAME
swiftj2k-cli \- JPEG 2000 Part 1, HTJ2K Part 15, JP3D Part 10 and JPIP Part 9 CLI for SwiftJ2K
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftj2k-cli
.RI [ options ] " command " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The standalone executable of the SwiftJ2K, SwiftJ2K3D and SwiftJ2KJPIP libraries.
It encodes unsigned and signed 1 to 16-bit greyscale, RGB, RGBA and
multi-component images (from NRRD, PGM, PPM, PNM, PNG, TIFF or RAW inputs) to
JPEG 2000 Part 1 (j2k) codestreams in lossless, near-lossless or lossy mode, or
to HTJ2K Part 15 (htj2k) codestreams, or wrapped in JP2 (jp2), JPH (jph) or JPX
(jpx) box containers; decodes Part 1 and Part 15 codestreams and JP2/JPH/JPX
containers to NRRD, PGM, PPM, PNM, PNG, TIFF or RAW; transcodes losslessly
between Part 1 and Part 15 codestreams and containers in the wavelet
coefficient domain without materialising an intermediate pixel image; inspects
and validates codestreams and containers; converts between uncompressed image
formats; compares 2D images and 3D volumes (MSE, MAE, MaxError, PSNR,
bit-exactness); batch-processes directories and file lists with bounded
concurrency; encodes and decodes 3D volumetric datasets (JP3D Part 10);
streams images over JPIP (Part 9 client and server); runs in-process
performance benchmarks; generates shell completion scripts; and reports the
library's capabilities. Build with Swift 6.2 or later (6.4 qualified) in
Swift 6 language mode. Apple OS minimum is 26.0.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encode \-i IMAGE \-o OUT.j2k [\-\-input-format nrrd|pgm|ppm|pnm|png|tiff|raw] [\-\-output-format j2k|htj2k|jp2|jph|jpx] [\-\-container codestream|jp2|jph|jpx] [CODEC OPTIONS]
Encode an uncompressed image to a Part 1 (j2k, default) or Part 15 (htj2k)
codestream or JP2 (jp2), JPH (jph) or JPX (jpx) container. Supported codec
options include \-\-container codestream|jp2|jph|jpx, \-\-mode
lossless|near-lossless|lossy (\-\-lossy shorthand), \-\-max-error E
(\-\-near-lossless E), \-\-quality Q (0.0..1.0), \-\-bpp RATE, \-\-layers N
(1..255), \-\-wavelet auto|53|97, \-\-mct auto|none|rct|ict, \-\-progression
lrcp|rlcp|rpcl|pcrl|cprl, \-\-tile-size WxH, \-\-precincts WxH, \-\-roi
X,Y,W,H[,SHIFT], \-\-guard-bits N (1..7), \-\-qstyle
auto|none|derived|expounded, \-\-sop, \-\-eph, \-\-levels N (0..32),
\-\-code-block WxH (powers of two 4..1024 with W*H <= 4096, default 64x64),
\-\-precision N (1..16), and for RAW inputs \-\-dimensions WxH, \-\-bit-depth N,
\-\-components N and \-\-signed.
.TP
.B decode \-i IN.j2k \-o IMAGE [\-\-output-format nrrd|pgm|ppm|pnm|png|tiff|raw]
Decode a Part 1 or HTJ2K codestream or JP2/JPH/JPX container to NRRD (default
for stdout or .nrrd), PGM, PPM, PNM, PNG, TIFF or RAW.
.TP
.B transcode \-i IN.j2k \-o OUT.j2c [\-\-input-format j2k|htj2k|jp2|jph|jpx] [\-\-output-format j2k|htj2k|jp2|jph|jpx] [\-\-container codestream|jp2|jph|jpx] [\-\-levels N] [\-\-code-block WxH]
Losslessly transcode between Part 1 (j2k/jp2/jpx) and Part 15 (htj2k/jph/jpx)
codestreams and containers in the wavelet coefficient domain without allocating
an intermediate pixel image or writing temporary image files.
.TP
.B inspect \-i IN.j2k [\-\-json]
Report geometry, precision and format from the container and codestream headers
without decoding samples; output on stdout as text or one JSON document.
.TP
.B validate \-i IN.j2k [\-\-json]
Fully decode in memory and report success or the defined failure; no output
file is written.
.TP
.B convert \-i IN \-o OUT [\-\-input-format FMT] [\-\-output-format FMT] [\-\-bit-depth 8|16]
Convert between uncompressed 2D image formats (nrrd, pgm, ppm, pnm, png, tiff,
raw) with optional 8-bit or 16-bit sample depth scaling.
.TP
.B compare \-i IMAGE_A \-r IMAGE_B [\-\-mode 2d|3d] [\-\-bit-exact] [\-\-max-error N] [\-\-min-psnr DB] [\-\-json]
Compare two 2D images or 3D volumes (compressed or uncompressed) and report
per-component and overall MSE, MAE, MaxError, PSNR and bit-exactness. Exits 3
if a requested threshold is not met.
.TP
.B batch encode|decode|transcode|encode3d|decode3d \-i DIR_OR_GLOB \-o OUT_DIR [\-\-input-list FILE] [\-\-recursive] [\-\-filter GLOB] [\-\-exclude GLOB] [\-\-output-suffix EXT] [\-\-threads 1..8] [\-\-continue-on-error] [\-\-progress] [\-\-json]
Process multiple inputs in parallel using a bounded worker pool.
.TP
.B encode3d \-i VOLUME_OR_SLICE_DIR \-o OUT.j3d [\-\-codec j2k-lossless|j2k-lossy|htj2k-lossless|htj2k-lossy] [\-\-tile-size WxHxD] [\-\-levels N|X,Y,Z] [\-\-progression lrcps|rlcps|pcrls|slrcp|cprls] [\-\-spacing X,Y,Z] [\-\-origin X,Y,Z] [\-\-slice-range START:END]
Encode a 3D NRRD volume, 3D RAW volume, or directory of 2D slices into a JP3D
(ISO/IEC 15444-10) volumetric codestream.
.TP
.B decode3d \-i IN.j3d \-o OUT_VOLUME_OR_DIR [\-\-output-format nrrd|raw|pgm|ppm|pnm|png|tiff] [\-\-region X,Y,Z,W,H,D] [\-\-slice-range START:END] [\-\-resolution-level R] [\-\-layers N] [\-\-slice-naming PATTERN]
Decode a JP3D volumetric codestream to a 3D NRRD/RAW volume or a directory of
2D slice images, with optional 3D ROI or Z-slice range decoding.
.TP
.B jpip client|server [\-\-server URL] [\-\-target NAME] [\-\-single-file PATH] [\-\-data-dir DIR] [\-\-port PORT] [\-\-region X,Y,W,H] [\-\-resolution-level R] [\-\-quality-layers N] [\-\-components C0,C1] [\-\-coding-preference none|htj2k|standard] [\-\-once] [\-\-json]
Stream JPEG 2000 / HTJ2K images interactively over JPIP (ISO/IEC 15444-9) or
serve a directory/file of targets.
.TP
.B benchmark \-i IMAGE [\-\-runs N] [\-\-warmup N] [\-\-encode-only] [\-\-decode-only] [\-\-htj2k] [\-\-compare-all] [\-\-format text|json|csv] [\-o FILE]
Run in-process encode and decode performance benchmarks with zero external
process invocations.
.TP
.B completions bash|zsh|fish
Emit a shell completion script to stdout.
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-json]
Report actual library encode/decode/inspect/transcode support. JSON is one
document on stdout.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show global or command-specific help. No arguments also show global help.
.TP
.B version
Show the development version.
.SH INPUT AND OUTPUT OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-input PATH
Input file or directory, or \- for standard input, which is read completely first.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output PATH
Final output file or directory, or \- for binary standard output. A file is
written to a sibling temporary file and renamed into place; an existing file is
refused (exit 6) unless \-\-overwrite is given; nothing partial remains after a
failure. Binary standard output cannot be rolled back and a closed pipe is
reported as exit 6.
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-reference PATH
Reference image or volume path for compare (or run count shorthand on benchmark).
.TP
.B \-\-input-format FMT, \-\-output-format FMT
Declare compressed (j2k, htj2k, jp2, jph, jpx) or uncompressed (nrrd, pgm, ppm,
pnm, png, tiff, raw) formats; a mismatch against the bytes is exit 4.
.TP
.B \-\-container codestream|jp2|jph|jpx
Selects the output container wrapper on encode and transcode.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Permit replacing an existing output file.
.TP
.B \-\-json
For inspect, validate, compare, batch, jpip and benchmark, a JSON document on
stdout. For encode, decode, transcode, convert, encode3d and decode3d, a JSON
report on stderr so that binary stdout stays clean.
.SH LIMIT AND POLICY OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode lossless|near-lossless|lossy|2d|3d
Selects the compression mode for encode/encode3d (default lossless) or comparison
dimensionality for compare (2d or 3d). Decode, validate and transcode accept
lossless only; near-lossless or lossy on those verbs returns 4.
.TP
.B \-\-backend auto|scalar|accelerated
Selects the execution backend (default auto). Unavailable or unknown backends return 4.
.TP
.B \-\-copy-policy require-sharing|allow-copy
Controls zero-copy storage sharing vs copying when importing/exporting buffers.
.TP
.B \-\-metadata-policy preserve|discard-ancillary
Controls ancillary metadata handling during decode and transcoding: preserve
(default) retains COM marker segments and ancillary container boxes (xml, uuid,
uinf, jp2i, asoc) within the metadata byte limit; discard-ancillary omits them.
.TP
.B \-\-threads N, \-\-max-memory BYTES, \-\-max-metadata BYTES, \-\-timeout SECONDS
Worker limit 1..8, admission budget in bytes for input, output and workspace,
admission budget in bytes for container and codestream metadata, and the
operation deadline (exit 5 when exceeded).
.SH NRRD PROFILE
Attached header ending in an empty line, magic NRRD0001 to NRRD0005, fields
type: uint8|int8|uint16|int16, dimension: 2 (sizes: W H), dimension: 3
(sizes: C W H, sizes: W H C with kinds, or sizes: W H D for 3D volumes) or
dimension: 4 (sizes: C W H D for multi-component 3D volumes), encoding: raw and
endian: little or big (for 16-bit types). The key swiftj2k.meaningfulbits:=N
(1..16) records the declared precision; decode always writes it. Detached data
files, line or byte skips, block sizes, other types, dimensions and encodings
are refused (exit 4); a mismatched data byte length is malformed (exit 3).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help, including after a command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the development version.
.TP
.B \-v, \-vv, \-vvv, \-vvvv, \-vvvvv
Increase diagnostic verbosity, up to 5.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose LEVEL, \-\-verbose=LEVEL
Set level to 1 through 5, or + through +++++. Bare verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-verbose: LEVEL, \-verbose:LEVEL
Equivalent explicit verbosity spelling; bare \-verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress optional diagnostics; errors remain visible. Conflicts with
verbosity.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC LEVELS
Default 0 reports errors only. Levels are cumulative:
1 summary; 2 stages; 3 capability/configuration details; 4 elapsed timing;
5 bounded trace. Invalid levels or totals above 5 return 2.
Explicit levels set and repeated flags increment in argument order.
Diagnostics use stderr. Requested help/version/capability/inspection data uses
stdout. No payload bytes, metadata, raw addresses or input/output paths are
logged.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 invalid usage or argument; 3 malformed input or failed comparison
threshold; 4 unsupported format, feature, layout or backend; 5 resource limit
or deadline; 6 I/O or storage failure, including an existing output without
\-\-overwrite and a closed pipe; 7 internal failure; 130 interrupted by SIGINT,
with nothing published.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
swiftj2k-cli encode \-i slice.nrrd \-o slice.j2k \-\-precision 12
swiftj2k-cli encode \-i slice.png \-o slice.jph \-\-output-format jph
swiftj2k-cli decode \-i slice.j2k \-o slice.tiff \-\-overwrite
swiftj2k-cli transcode \-i source.j2k \-\-input-format j2k \-\-output-format htj2k \-\-mode lossless \-o converted.j2c
swiftj2k-cli convert \-i slice.pgm \-o slice.png
swiftj2k-cli compare \-i original.pgm \-r decoded.png \-\-bit-exact \-\-json
swiftj2k-cli batch encode \-i ./slices \-o ./encoded \-\-filter '*.pgm' \-\-threads 4
swiftj2k-cli encode3d \-i ./slices \-o volume.j3d \-\-codec htj2k-lossless
swiftj2k-cli decode3d \-i volume.j3d \-o volume.nrrd \-\-region 0,0,0,64,64,16
swiftj2k-cli jpip client \-\-single-file image.jp2 \-o preview.png \-\-json
swiftj2k-cli benchmark \-i slice.nrrd \-\-runs 5 \-\-compare-all \-\-json
swiftj2k-cli completions zsh
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
Scripts/install-cli.sh installs or updates the executable and this page
together.
Use \-\-prefix for an absolute prefix (default /usr/local), \-\-destdir or
DESTDIR
for staging, and \-\-binary for a prebuilt binary matching VERSION.
Files are PREFIX/bin/swiftj2k-cli and PREFIX/share/man/man1/swiftj2k-cli.1.
For custom prefixes use man \-M PREFIX/share/man swiftj2k-cli, or configure
MANPATH.
No index refresh is needed for direct lookup; no sudo runs automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
.PP
CLI.md, TRANSCODING.md, Documentation/MILESTONE8.md, Documentation/MILESTONE9.md and Documentation/MILESTONE12.md in the SwiftJ2K repository.
